id: pmc-q22j
title: This package generates its own changelog without the flag that stops the heading date coming from the clock
description: "pm-changelog synthesises a pending release window for a version with no matching git tag and stamps it with the current UTC date. Its own changelog scripts and release workflow did not pass the date-from-version flag, the one this package itself ships for exactly that case, so its changelog check regenerates a different heading date every day and fails on any day after the changelog was written. Applied the flag to every invocation of the generator here: two sites in package.json and one in the release workflow."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 1
tags[3]: changelog,gates,release
created_at: "2026-08-24T09:42:16.204Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-26T18:42:06.810Z"
deadline: "2026-08-31T00:00:00.000Z"
assignee: "harness:claude-code"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 30
acceptance_criteria: "Every invocation of the generator in this package passes the flag, and changelog check passes on a day other than the version's own calendar date"
dependencies[1]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
  pmc-ilrh,related,"2026-08-24T09:42:16.204Z","harness:claude-code","cli:create:dep",detected
comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-24T09:42:16.204Z","harness:claude-code",Found while rolling this fix across the fleet; this package was exposed to the defect it fixes for everyone else.
  "2026-08-24T10:06:41.071Z","harness:claude-code","CodeRabbit was right that the linked test only covered the package.json invocation and never reached the direct pm-changelog commands in the release workflow. Added an executable check that does both halves. The static half enumerates every tracked file containing a generator invocation and asserts each file's flagged count is not below its site count, which fails when any single site loses the flag; verified by removing the flag from one of two release.yml sites and watching it report one of two and exit non-zero. The behavioural half runs the generator twice on the same probe version 2026.1.2, deliberately chosen so its calendar date cannot coincide with today, and asserts the heading is 2026.1.2 - 2026-01-02 with the flag and 2026.1.2 - 2026-08-24 without it, so the test states the defect rather than merely asserting the fix."
  "2026-08-26T18:42:02.455Z",pi-agent,"Release workflow fix: replaced the two hand-rolled node dist/cli.js invocations in the \"Build and generate changelog\" step of .github/workflows/release.yml with 'npm run changelog:full' and 'npm run changelog:check'. The hand-rolled calls passed --version but omitted --date-from-version, --respect-item-release and the unbounded --output-budget/--output-limit args that changelog:full carries, so the release commit wrote a clock-dated CHANGELOG.md while npm run changelog:check (CI, release:check) regenerated with --date-from-version and could then fail on a later unrelated commit on main. The \"Update release version\" step already runs npm version before this step, so --release-version-from-package in the scripts resolves to the release being cut. --github-step-summary was dropped because changelog:full has no such flag; reintroducing it would mean a third hand-rolled invocation and the drift it caused. Also aligned the RELEASE_NOTES.md generator invocation (~line 697) with release:notes in package.json by adding --respect-item-release and the unbounded --output-budget/--output-limit args it was missing. Extended scripts/verify-release-changelog-date.sh with a section that fails if any direct node dist/cli.js block in release.yml omits --date-from-version, and confirms the step delegates to the npm scripts; verified non-vacuous by reverting the workflow fix (exit 1) and restoring it (exit 0)."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-24T09:42:16.204Z","harness:claude-code","Site audit after the change: package.json 2 of 2 flagged, release.yml 1 of 1 flagged."
learnings[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-24T09:42:16.204Z","harness:claude-code",A package that ships a remedy is not automatically a package that applies it; the rollout has to include the origin repo.
  "2026-08-26T18:42:06.809Z",pi-agent,"Generate-vs-check drift class: when a release workflow hand-rolls a generator invocation separate from the package.json scripts that CI and release:check use, the two diverge silently. The workflow commits a CHANGELOG.md generated with one flag set (e.g. the UTC clock date fallback) while changelog:check regenerates with another (--date-from-version), and a later changelog:check on main fails on a commit that never touched the changelog. The remedy is to never hand-roll the invocation in the workflow: delegate to the same npm script for both generation and check, so there is exactly one source of truth for the flag set. A regression test must key on the direct node dist/cli.js call sites (not on --release-version-from-package, which the hand-rolled call may omit in favour of --version) or it will not catch the drift."
files[3]:
  - path: package.json
    scope: project
  - path: .github/workflows/release.yml
    scope: project
    note: the release workflow's generator invocation now derives the no-tag date from the calendar version
  - path: scripts/verify-release-changelog-date.sh
    scope: project
    note: "executable proof for the release workflow invocations, which the package.json changelog check never reaches"
tests[2]:
  - command: "npm run changelog:check"
    scope: project
  - command: bash scripts/verify-release-changelog-date.sh
    path: scripts/verify-release-changelog-date.sh
    scope: project
    note: "exercises the release workflow path that npm run changelog:check does not: asserts every generator invocation in every tracked file carries the flag, and shows the same probe version yielding its own calendar date with the flag and today's date without it"
docs[1]{path,scope,note}:
  "https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/blob/main/README.md",project,flag reference
body: "The release workflow tags only after npm publish succeeds. Publish has failed fleet wide since 2026-08-21, so this package carries an untagged version and sits on the clock dependent path its own flag exists to remove."
